C03: a helper process under the application's own install tree counts for the launch (APPS1609)

APPS1607 measured that «Abre Steam» starts the owner's Steam client and its window appears, but the product reports verification_failed: the visible window belongs to steamwebhelper.exe, a helper steam.exe starts from its own install tree, and NotepadIdentityPolicy.IsAllowed counted only the bootstrap executable. A process whose executable lives under the target's install directory is now the same application for the launch observation — never when that directory is the Windows directory, a Program Files root or WindowsApps, where unrelated processes share the tree — so the helper's window verifies the launch and the receipt keeps one consistent process and window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


